# Citation metadata for Court Value.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Court Value scores or methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "Court Value (CV): a historically portable NBA/ABA player-season value metric"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - given-names: Mario
    family-names: Tavolieri
    name-suffix: III
abstract: >-
  Court Value (CV) is a regular-season player × season × league metric for the NBA
  (1952–present) and ABA (1968–1976). It measures realized season value and
  responsibility from 1952-available box-score production, games-played team margin
  of victory and a bounded team-defense responsibility credit, standardized within each
  league-season. It is not a causal impact or wins-above-replacement estimate.
keywords:
  - basketball
  - NBA
  - ABA
  - Court Value
  - player evaluation
  - sports analytics
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
